  "grammar": [
    {
      "id": "b3_u06_l2_g1",
      "pattern": "A-(으)ㄴ데, V-는데, N인데 (vaziyat → iltimos/savol)",
      "meaning_uz": "..., (shuning uchun) ...: vaziyatni aytib, so'rash",
      "meaning_en": "Setting up a situation before a request or question",
      "explanation_md": "3-2 da **-는데** fon berardi. Bu yerda u **vaziyatni tushuntirib**, keyin **iltimos, savol yoki taklif** qilish uchun ishlatiladi — telefon va xizmat suhbatlarida juda ko'p.\n\n**세탁기가 고장 났는데 언제 와 주실 수 있어요?** — *Kir mashinasi buzildi, qachon kela olasiz?*\n\n### Qanday yasaladi (3-2 bilan bir xil)\n\n- Fe'l → **-는데**, o'tgan → **-았/었는데**: 고장 **났는데**\n- Sifat → **-(으)ㄴ데**: 이상**한데**, 추**운데**\n- Ot → **N인데**: 처음**인데**\n\n### Odatiy tuzilma\n\n**[vaziyat]-는데 + [iltimos/savol]**\n\n- **물이 새는데 좀 봐 주시겠어요?** — *Suv oqyapti, bir qarab bera olasizmi?*\n- **처음인데 어떻게 해요?** — *Birinchi marta, qanday qilinadi?*\n- **보일러가 안 되는데 오늘 오실 수 있어요?** — *Qozon ishlamayapti, bugun kela olasizmi?*\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- Gap **-는데요** bilan tugasa — yumshoq ishora: **세탁기가 고장 났는데요…** — *Kir mashinasi buzilgan edi…* (javobni kutish)",
      "explanation_md_en": "In 3-2, **-는데** set up background. Here it **explains a situation** and then leads into a **request, question or suggestion** — very common on the phone and in service calls.\n\n**세탁기가 고장 났는데 언제 와 주실 수 있어요?** — *The washing machine broke — when can you come?*\n\n### How to form it (same as 3-2)\n\n- Verb → **-는데**, past → **-았/었는데**: 고장 **났는데**\n- Adjective → **-(으)ㄴ데**: 이상**한데**, 추**운데**\n- Noun → **N인데**: 처음**인데**\n\n### Typical pattern\n\n**[situation]-는데 + [request/question]**\n\n- **물이 새는데 좀 봐 주시겠어요?** — *It's leaking — could you take a look?*\n- **처음인데 어떻게 해요?** — *It's my first time — how do I do it?*\n- **보일러가 안 되는데 오늘 오실 수 있어요?** — *The boiler isn't working — can you come today?*\n\n### Remember\n\n- Ending a sentence with **-는데요** is a soft hint: **세탁기가 고장 났는데요…** — *The washing machine's broken…* (waiting for help)",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "Fe'l",
          "condition_en": "Verb",
          "rule": "V-는데 / V-았/었는데",
          "example": "새는데, 고장 났는데"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Sifat",
          "condition_en": "Adjective",
          "rule": "A-(으)ㄴ데",
          "example": "이상한데, 추운데"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Ot",
          "condition_en": "Noun",
          "rule": "N인데",
          "example": "처음인데"
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
